  "functions": [
    "FUNC.PERMUT"
  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "PERMUT evaluates an ascending x87 double-rounded product from n - k + 1 to n, not n! / (n - k)!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, PERMUT(number, number_chosen) truncates both arguments toward zero (rejecting n < 0, k < 0, k > n, or overflow with #NUM!) and accumulates the ascending x87 PC64-to-PC53 double-rounded product acc = RN53(RN64(acc * f)) for f = n - k + 1 ..= n. Evaluating n! / (n - k)! instead overflows early for large n and misses PERMUT(61, 20) by 1 ULP. All 3,432 full-bank PERMUT rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 3,432/3,432 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PERMUT rows plus the PERMUT(61, 20) pin.",
